msgstr "Róża"

msgid ""
"Rose: a soft music box tune with a rustle of petals. A rose drifting in the "
"Valentine's season, worth 25 more than a heart."
msgstr ""
"Róża: cicha melodia pozytywki z szelestem płatków. Róża dryfująca w okresie "
"walentynkowym, warta 25 więcej niż serce."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid ""
"a soft music box tune with a rustle of petals. A rose drifting in the "
"Valentine's season, worth 25 more than a heart."
msgstr ""
"cicha melodia pozytywki z szelestem płatków. Róża dryfująca w okresie "
"walentynkowym, warta 25 więcej niż serce."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Golden heart"
msgstr "Złote serce"

msgid ""
"Golden heart: a shimmer of tiny bells. Only on Valentine's night, worth 100."
msgstr ""
"Złote serce: migotanie malutkich dzwoneczków. Tylko w Walentynkową noc, "
"warte 100."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a shimmer of tiny bells. Only on Valentine's night, worth 100."
msgstr ""
"migotanie malutkich dzwoneczków. Tylko w Walentynkową noc, warte 100."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Love note"
msgstr "Liścik miłosny"

msgid ""
"Love note: a slow flutter of paper. A folded note drifting slowly. Hit it "
"to keep the note."
msgstr ""
"Liścik miłosny: powolny trzepot papieru. Złożony liścik powoli dryfuje. "
"Traf go, by go zachować."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid ""
"a slow flutter of paper. A folded note drifting slowly. Hit it to keep the "
"note."
msgstr ""
"powolny trzepot papieru. Złożony liścik powoli dryfuje. Traf go, by go "
"zachować."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "String creak"
msgstr "Skrzypienie cięciwy"

msgid "String creak: the bow drawing, rising as the string comes back."
msgstr ""
"Skrzypienie cięciwy: łuk się napina, dźwięk rośnie, gdy cięciwa się cofa."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "the bow drawing, rising as the string comes back."
msgstr "łuk się napina, dźwięk rośnie, gdy cięciwa się cofa."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Full draw"
msgstr "Pełne naciągnięcie"

msgid "Full draw: a soft wooden click. Let go now to shoot."
msgstr ""
"Pełne naciągnięcie: ciche drewniane kliknięcie. Puść teraz, by strzelić."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a soft wooden click. Let go now to shoot."
msgstr "ciche drewniane kliknięcie. Puść teraz, by strzelić."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Arrow loosed"
msgstr "Wypuszczona strzała"

msgid "Arrow loosed: a twang and a whoosh."
msgstr "Wypuszczona strzała: brzdęk i świst."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a twang and a whoosh."
msgstr "brzdęk i świst."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Slack string"
msgstr "Luźna cięciwa"

msgid ""
"Slack string: a dull flop. Let go too soon, so the arrow stays in your hand."
msgstr ""
"Luźna cięciwa: głuche klapnięcie. Puszczono za wcześnie, więc strzała "
"zostaje w dłoni."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a dull flop. Let go too soon, so the arrow stays in your hand."
msgstr ""
"głuche klapnięcie. Puszczono za wcześnie, więc strzała zostaje w dłoni."

msgid "Aim tick: the bow turns one step."
msgstr "Tyknięcie celowania: łuk obraca się o jeden krok."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "the bow turns one step."
msgstr "łuk obraca się o jeden krok."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Edge knock"
msgstr "Stuknięcie na krańcu"

msgid "Edge knock: the bow is turned as far as it goes."
msgstr "Stuknięcie na krańcu: łuk jest obrócony do oporu."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "the bow is turned as far as it goes."
msgstr "łuk jest obrócony do oporu."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Empty quiver"
msgstr "Pusty kołczan"

msgid "Empty quiver: a hollow tap of wood."
msgstr "Pusty kołczan: głuche stuknięcie drewna."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a hollow tap of wood."
msgstr "głuche stuknięcie drewna."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Pop"
msgstr "Pęknięcie"

msgid "Pop: a paper heart bursts."
msgstr "Pęknięcie: papierowe serce pęka."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a paper heart bursts."
msgstr "papierowe serce pęka."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Sweetheart chord"
msgstr "Akord zakochanych"

msgid ""
"Sweetheart chord: rising chimes that end in a chord. Both hearts of a pair, "
"one after the other."
msgstr ""
"Akord zakochanych: rosnące dzwonki zakończone akordem. Oba serca z pary, "
"jedno po drugim."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid ""
"rising chimes that end in a chord. Both hearts of a pair, one after the "
"other."
msgstr ""
"rosnące dzwonki zakończone akordem. Oba serca z pary, jedno po drugim."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Rose caught"
msgstr "Złapana róża"

msgid "Rose caught: a rustle and a bright harp run."
msgstr "Złapana róża: szelest i jasny pasaż harfy."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a rustle and a bright harp run."
msgstr "szelest i jasny pasaż harfy."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Golden heart caught"
msgstr "Złapane złote serce"

msgid "Golden heart caught: a burst of bells, high and bright."
msgstr "Złapane złote serce: wybuch dzwonków, wysoki i jasny."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a burst of bells, high and bright."
msgstr "wybuch dzwonków, wysoki i jasny."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
